pipeline.library/AddUserXData                   pipeline.library/AddUserXData

    NAME
        AddUserXData -- Adds/Replaces some infomation to a users Extra Data
                            file.

    SYNOPSIS
        success = AddUserXData( user, data, type, length )
          d0                     a0    a1    d0     d1

        BOOL AddUserXData( struct User *, APTR, ULONG, ULONG );

    FUNCTION
        Zeus can store extra information for a user other than the standard
        user structure.  The stored data will not be processed in any way
        by Zeus, it will be stored verbatim.  There is no limit on the
        length of data stored other than memory/disk constraints.
        
        This function will add data to the users XData list.  If the type
        already exists, it will be replaced.
        
    EXAMPLE
    
        /* Load a user called 'Test User' and add some XData */
        
        #define ID_TEST     MAKE_ID('T','E','S','T')

        struct User *u;
        UBYTE        data[10];
        
        if( u = LoadUser( "Test User" ) )
        {
           if( LoadUserXData( u ) > 0 )
           {
              if( AddUserXData( u, data, ID_TEST, 10 ) )
              {
                  printf( "Success!\n" );
              }
              else
              {
                  printf( "Out of memory!\n" );
              }
           
              SaveUser( u );
           }
           UnLoadUser( u );
        }
    
    INPUTS
        user   - User pointer as obtained by LoadUser(), LoadUserFromKey(),
                    or MakeNewUser().
        data   - Pointer to the data to be added.
        type   - The datas ID code.
        length - The number of bytes to be added.
    
    RESULTS
        TRUE  - Data was added.
        FALSE - Out of memory.
        
    NOTES
        NEVER use a user pointer not obtained from the LoadUser functions.
        
        The ID for the data should be created using the MAKE_ID macro as in
           the example above.

        The XData added will not be saved until a SaveUser() call.
        
        You must call LoadUserXData() before the XData routines will work.
    
    SEE ALSO
        LoadUser(), LoadUserFromKey(), MakeNewUser(), SaveUser(),
        UnLoadUser(), RemUserXData(), GetUserXData(), GetUserXDataSize()

