pipeline.library/ChatWrite                         pipeline.library/ChatWrite

    NAME
        ChatWrite -- Write data to a line while it's in chat mode.

    SYNOPSIS
        success = ChatWrite( LineNum, Data, Length )
          d0                    d0     a0     d1

        BOOL ChatWrite( UWORD, APTR, ULONG );

    FUNCTION
        When in chat mode, all normal write commands will block so this
        function is provided for writing in chat mode.  It will detect
        whether the line is in chat mode so it's always safe to call.

    INPUTS
        LineNum - Number of the line to write to.
        Data    - The data to write.
        Length  - Length of the data.

    RESULTS
        TRUE  - Data was written
        FALSE - The line doesn't exist or the line is not in chat mode or
                there was another kind of error.

    BUGS
        None.

    SEE ALSO
        StartChat(), StopChat()
