pipeline.library/ExpandCC                           pipeline.library/ExpandCC

    NAME
        ExpandCC -- Expand a control code into a buffer.

    SYNOPSIS
        length = ExpandCC( LineNum, CC, Buffer, MaxLen )
          d0                  d0    a0    a1      d1
          
        int ExpandCC( int, char *, char *, int );

    FUNCTION
        With this function you can get the contents of any control code
        held in any part of Pipeline.

    INPUTS
       LineNum - Line number.
       CC      - String pointer to a normally formatted PL control code.
       Buffer  - Where to put the data.
       MaxLen  - Length of the buffer.

    RESULTS
       0 - Control code isn't supported.
      >0 - Length of the returned data.

    BUGS
       Doesn't take much notice of the MaxLen argument!

pipeline.library/FileXfer                           pipeline.library/FileXfer

    NAME
        FileXfer -- Transfer files from/to the user.

    SYNOPSIS
        info = FileXfer( Mode, Protocol, Filenames, Line )
         d0               d0      d1        a0       a1


        struct XferInfo *FileXfer( ULONG, ULONG, char *, struct Line * );

    FUNCTION
        Sends/Receives one or more files to the user online.  FileNames
        contains a list of zero or more file names to transfer separated
        by a single space.

        Sending:
           You must specify at least one filename when sending.  All
           filenames given must include their full path.

        Receiving:
           If the protocol has a batch capability then you do not need to
           specify the filenames, give NULL for the FileNames parameter.

           All files received are put in File:Uploadx/ (where x is the
           number of the line).

    INPUTS
        Mode      - XFER_SEND for sending files or XFER_RECEIVE for
                    receiving.
        Protocol  - The number of the file transfer protocol as defined
                    with Prefs/PLFileCfg.
        FileNames - Files to transfer or NULL.
        Line      - Pointer to the line structure to transfer the files on.
        
    RESULTS
         0 - Error setting up transfer.
        >0 - Pointer to a XferInfo structure which tells you how the
             transfer went.

    SEE ALSO
        FreeXferInfo()

