pipeline.library/GetLineStatus                 pipeline.library/GetLineStatus

    NAME
        GetLineStatus -- Obtain flags from a line.

    SYNOPSIS
        Flags = GetLineStatus( LineNum )
          d0                      d0
        
        ULONG GetLineStatus( UWORD );

    FUNCTION
        Returns some flags from the line structure that Pipeline uses
        internally and are therefore read only.  With these flags you can
        find whether the line is local or not and whether the user is in a
        door among others.

    INPUTS
        LineNum - Number of the line to get the flags from.

    RESULTS
        Flags - See libraries/pipeline.h for flag definitions.  Returns
                NULL if the line doesn't exist.

    BUGS
        None.

    SEE ALSO
        GetLine()
pipeline.library/GetShared                         pipeline.library/GetShared

    NAME
        GetShared -- Returns a pointer to the SharedData structure.

    SYNOPSIS
        Shared = GetShared()
          D0

        struct SharedData *GetShared( void );

    FUNCTION
        Gets the pointer to the Shared Data.  This structure contains
        library bases which you can get and use in your own programs.  They
        will always be valid while Pipeline is running.  This structure
        should be READ ONLY!!!

    INPUTS
        None.

    RESULTS
         0 - Pipeline is not running.
        >0 - Pointer to the shared data.

    BUGS
        None.

pipeline.library/GetUserXData                   pipeline.library/GetUserXData

    NAME
        GetUserXData -- Gets some infomation from a users Extra Data file.

    SYNOPSIS
        reallength = GetUserXData( user, buffer, type, length, offset )
            d0                      a0     a1     d0     d1      d2

        ULONG GetUserXData( struct User *, APTR, ULONG, ULONG, ULONG );

    FUNCTION
        If the specified type of XData exists for the given user, it will
        be copied into the supplied buffer.  If there is more data than
        buffer space, only 'length' bytes will be copied.  You can find
        out how big an XData entry is with GetUserXDataSize().
        
    INPUTS
        user   - User pointer as obtained by LoadUser(), LoadUserFromKey(),
                    or MakeNewUser().
        buffer - Buffer to receive the data.
        type   - The datas ID code.
        length - The size of the buffer.
        offset - Number of bytes into the data to start reading at.
    
    RESULTS
        0 - Data ID could not be found
       >0 - Length of data copied.  Will be less than or equal to your
               buffers size.
        
    NOTES
        NEVER use a user pointer not obtained from the LoadUser functions.
        
        The buffer will not be null terminated.  Watch out for this if you
        are storing strings.
    
    SEE ALSO
        AddUserXData(), RemUserXData(), GetUserXDataSize()

pipeline.library/GetUserXDataSize           pipeline.library/GetUserXDataSize

    NAME
        GetUserXDataSize -- Finds out the length of an item of XData.

    SYNOPSIS
        length = GetUserXDataSize( user, type )
          d0                        a0    d0

        ULONG GetUserXDataSize( struct User *, ULONG );

    FUNCTION
        Returns the length of a stored XData item.
        
    INPUTS
        user   - User pointer as obtained by LoadUser(), LoadUserFromKey(),
                    or MakeNewUser().
        type   - The datas ID code.
    
    RESULTS
        0 - Data ID could not be found
       >0 - Length of XData item.
        
    NOTES
