                      down.

    SYNOPSIS
        success = LineKillMe( Line, SigBits )
          d0                   d0     d1
          
        int LineKillMe( UWORD, ULONG );

    FUNCTION
        As for pipeline.library/KillMe except you will be signalled when
        the specified line is closing down.
        
    INPUTS
        Line    - The line number in question.
        SigBits - The mask of bits that your task will be sent.

    RESULTS
       FALSE - Not sucessful.
       TRUE  - Task installed in list.

    BUGS

    SEE ALSO
       KillMe(), DontKillMe(), LineDontKillMe()
pipeline.library/LineLogWrite                   pipeline.library/LineLogWrite

    NAME
        LineLogWrite -- Write some data to a lines log file.

    SYNOPSIS
        LineLogWrite( LineNum, Type, Text )
                        d0      d1    a0
        
        void LineLogWrite( UWORD, char, char * );

    FUNCTION
        Will write the supplied text to the log file of the line 'LineNum'.
        What Type character you use is totally up to you and will be output
        as the first character in the log line followed by the date and
        time and then the 'Text'.  The text will have a carrage return
        added to the end of it.
        
    EXAMPLE
        LineLogWrite( 0, 'i', "This is an information line" );
        
        Will write "i 25-Nov-93 16:04:40 | This is an information line" to
        'Logs:Line-0.Log'

    INPUTS

    RESULTS
        None.

    BUGS
        None.

