pipeline.library/SpaceToUnder                   pipeline.library/SpaceToUnder

    NAME
        SpaceToUnder -- Converts all spaces in a string to underscores.

    SYNOPSIS
        SpaceToUnder( String )
                        A0
                        
        void SpaceToUnder( char * );

    FUNCTION
        Converts all spaces in the given string to underscores which can be
        useful when accessing the users directory.

    EXAMPLE
       struct User *user;
       char   name[80];
       BPTR   file;
       
       sprintf( (char *)&name, "USER:%s/My-Prog.dat", &user->ur_Name );
       SpaceToUnder( &name );

       /* 'name' now looks like:

                 'USER:Person_With_Many_Middle_Names/My-Prog.dat'
       */

       file = Open( name, MODE_NEWFILE );
           
        :        :
           
       Close( file );

    INPUTS
       String - Pointer to the null terminated string which is to be
                   converted.

    RESULTS
       None.

    BUGS
       None.

    SEE ALSO
       UnderToSpace()
pipeline.library/StartChat                         pipeline.library/StartChat

    NAME
        StartChat -- Puts the line into chat mode.

    SYNOPSIS
        success = StartChat( LineNum, Hook )
          d0                    d0     a0

        BOOL StartChat( UWORD, BOOL (*)(struct Line *, struct ChatChar *) );

    FUNCTION
        This function provides an easy way to make your own chat program.
        Once the line is in chat mode, your hook function will be called
        every time a character is typed.  You can also decern whether the
        character came from the SysOp or the User by looking in the
        ChatChar structure.

    INPUTS
        LineNum - Number of the line to start chat on.
        Hook    - Your chat hook which will be called everytime there is an
                  input made on the line.  See SimpleChat.c for an example
                  of how to code a chat hook function.

    RESULTS
        TRUE  - Chat started.
        FALSE - Chat could not be started.

    NOTES
        Once the chat has started, this call will return immediately so you
        should Wait() until it has finished.  See the example simplechat
        source.

    BUGS
        None.

    SEE ALSO
        ChatWrite(), StopChat()
pipeline.library/StopChat                           pipeline.library/StopChat

    NAME
        StopChat -- Stops a chat and resumes normal operations.

    SYNOPSIS
        StopChat( LineNum )
                     d0

        void StopChat( UWORD );

    FUNCTION
        If the line is in chat mode it will return to normal operation.  A
        chat character will be sent to the chats hook function with
        'TYPE_FINISH' as it's type.  The hook should exit with a FALSE
        return code upon receipt of this code.

    INPUTS
        LineNum - Number of the line.

    RESULTS
        None.

    NOTES
        Safe to call from another task.  Safe to call when not in chat
        mode.

    BUGS
        None.

    SEE ALSO
        StartChat(), ChatWrite()
