pipeline.library/WriteLine                         pipeline.library/WriteLine

    NAME
        WriteLine -- Write some data to a line.

    SYNOPSIS
        code = WriteLine( LineNum, Data, Length, Flags )
         d0                 d0     a0     d1     d2

        LONG WriteLine( int, char *, int, int );

    FUNCTION

    INPUTS
       LineNum - The number of the line to write to.
       Data    - Pointer to the data to print.
       Length  - Length of the data.
       Flags   - See 'libraries/pipeline.h' - WF_* flags.

    RESULTS
       1 - Success.
       0 - No data to write.
      -1 - Data not shown - Flags included WF_ISMENU and user was in expert
              mode.
      -2 - User broke output (when flags include WF_BREAK)
      -3 - Flags included WF_SPECIALMORE and users screen length was
              reached.
      -4 - Carrier lost.
      -5 - User broke output at More? Y/N prompt.
      -6 - The line number that was given doesn't exist.

    BUGS

    SEE ALSO
        ChatWrite(), ReadLine()
